1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:07,973
If you ever have to hit a man to save your life, and you go for his face with your fist, the first bone that breaks may be your own.

2
00:00:08,673 --> 00:00:13,186
In my old life, there was a bone setter in Nada named Doctor Ishikawa.

3
00:00:13,287 --> 00:00:17,633
He worked out of a back room behind a pharmacy, and he never asked questions.

4
00:00:17,733 --> 00:00:22,862
One winter, in 1996, he set the hands of eleven of my young men.

5
00:00:22,961 --> 00:00:23,665
Eleven.

6
00:00:23,765 --> 00:00:25,674
Strong boys, every one of them.

7
00:00:25,774 --> 00:00:30,850
He told me, "Kuroda-san, your boys keep fighting with the smallest bones they own."

8
00:00:31,550 --> 00:00:36,411
Now, last week I told you to put the heel of your palm under a big man's nose.

9
00:00:36,511 --> 00:00:38,405
I am not taking back one word.

10
00:00:38,505 --> 00:00:40,108
But a palm is not a fist.

11
00:00:40,207 --> 00:00:47,125
And today I will show you exactly when going for the head makes sense, and when it is the most foolish thing you can do.

12
00:00:47,225 --> 00:00:53,173
You will learn three spots on a big man's body that can drop him, with no gloves and no great strength.

13
00:00:53,274 --> 00:00:58,943
And stay with me to the end, because there is one thing on his body that tells you which spot to choose.

14
00:00:59,042 --> 00:01:00,365
It is not his face.

15
00:01:00,466 --> 00:01:02,121
Almost nobody looks at it.

16
00:01:02,820 --> 00:01:04,289
I'm Reiko Kuroda.

17
00:01:04,390 --> 00:01:08,219
For thirty-five years, I was Yakuza, the Japanese mafia.

18
00:01:08,319 --> 00:01:10,947
I was the woman people like you were afraid of.

19
00:01:11,048 --> 00:01:12,815
It paid well, and it was wrong.

20
00:01:12,915 --> 00:01:16,965
But I knew exactly which people we picked, and which ones we left alone.

21
00:01:17,066 --> 00:01:19,924
Now, I teach it to the people we used to target.

22
00:01:20,025 --> 00:01:21,489
Not because you were weak.

23
00:01:21,590 --> 00:01:23,338
Because nobody ever showed you.

24
00:01:24,039 --> 00:01:24,864
Picture it.

25
00:01:24,965 --> 00:01:25,919
No gloves.

26
00:01:26,019 --> 00:01:27,043
No referee.

27
00:01:27,144 --> 00:01:29,965
You swing at his face, and he moves his head an inch.

28
00:01:30,066 --> 00:01:31,853
Your knuckles land on his forehead.

29
00:01:31,953 --> 00:01:34,071
The front of a man's skull is a helmet.

30
00:01:34,171 --> 00:01:35,814
It was built to take a blow.

31
00:01:35,915 --> 00:01:40,152
Your hand has twenty-seven small bones, and they were built to button a shirt.

32
00:01:40,253 --> 00:01:45,454
Boxers punch heads all night, but they wrap their hands in tape and pad them in gloves.

33
00:01:45,555 --> 00:01:46,710
You will have neither.

34
00:01:46,811 --> 00:01:49,603
And past sixty, our bones are thinner than they were.

35
00:01:49,703 --> 00:01:54,723
A broken hand in the first second means you have no hands at all for the rest of it.

36
00:01:55,424 --> 00:01:57,199
And here is the worst outcome.

37
00:01:57,299 --> 00:01:59,019
Say your punch lands perfectly.

38
00:01:59,120 --> 00:02:01,981
He falls backward, and his head hits the concrete.

39
00:02:02,081 --> 00:02:04,275
Now it is not self-defense anymore.

40
00:02:04,376 --> 00:02:10,375
A young man in my group threw one punch outside Sannomiya Station in 1999.

41
00:02:10,474 --> 00:02:11,355
One punch.

42
00:02:11,455 --> 00:02:12,320
One curb.

43
00:02:12,420 --> 00:02:13,698
He did six years.

44
00:02:13,798 --> 00:02:15,968
So the first rule is the oldest one.

45
00:02:16,068 --> 00:02:18,069
If you can walk away, you walk away.

46
00:02:18,169 --> 00:02:21,750
Only if he takes that choice from you, do you need what comes next.

47
00:02:22,449 --> 00:02:24,990
My young men counted on one thing in a fight.

48
00:02:25,091 --> 00:02:28,137
They counted on the other person swinging at their face.

49
00:02:28,236 --> 00:02:30,268
Because a face is easy to protect.

50
00:02:30,367 --> 00:02:31,748
Hands up, chin down.

51
00:02:31,848 --> 00:02:32,460
Done.

52
00:02:32,561 --> 00:02:34,519
What they could not protect was lower.

53
00:02:35,219 --> 00:02:36,209
Number three.

54
00:02:36,308 --> 00:02:37,069
The liver.

55
00:02:37,169 --> 00:02:40,806
Put your right hand on your right side, just below your bottom ribs.

56
00:02:40,907 --> 00:02:41,945
Press in a little.

57
00:02:42,045 --> 00:02:42,924
Feel that?

58
00:02:43,024 --> 00:02:45,842
Something uncomfortable, and no muscle over it.

59
00:02:45,943 --> 00:02:51,139
That is your liver, and every man has one in the same place, no matter how big he is.

60
00:02:51,240 --> 00:02:54,230
A big man's chest and stomach are like hitting a bear.

61
00:02:54,330 --> 00:02:56,948
Muscle, ribs, maybe a good layer of fat.

62
00:02:57,048 --> 00:03:01,112
But every suit of armor has a gap, and this is the gap on his body.

63
00:03:01,212 --> 00:03:05,675
Boxers with stomachs like steel go down from one well-placed blow there.

64
00:03:05,776 --> 00:03:06,972
They cannot help it.

65
00:03:07,073 --> 00:03:08,781
The body simply sits down.

66
00:03:09,481 --> 00:03:11,236
Here is how, after sixty.

67
00:03:11,336 --> 00:03:12,719
You do not need a fist.

68
00:03:12,819 --> 00:03:15,751
Use the heel of your palm, or up close, your elbow.

69
00:03:15,852 --> 00:03:20,092
Turn your hips into it, the way you turn to close a heavy car door with your hip.

70
00:03:20,193 --> 00:03:22,777
The power comes from that turn, not from your arm.

71
00:03:22,877 --> 00:03:24,424
And two mistakes to avoid.

72
00:03:24,524 --> 00:03:25,645
Do not wind up.

73
00:03:25,746 --> 00:03:31,608
A big swing, or a dip of your shoulder before you strike, tells him it is coming, and he will cover it.

74
00:03:31,707 --> 00:03:33,000
And do not hit the skin.

75
00:03:33,099 --> 00:03:37,735
Aim a few inches inside him, like you are reaching for something behind his ribs.

76
00:03:37,836 --> 00:03:40,201
A blow that stops at the skin is a slap.

77
00:03:40,301 --> 00:03:43,075
A blow that goes through is the one that drops him.

78
00:03:43,776 --> 00:03:46,188
Uncle Mori taught me this when I was fourteen.

79
00:03:46,288 --> 00:03:51,924
There was a student named Kuribayashi, a carpenter's son, so wide he filled the doorway.

80
00:03:52,024 --> 00:03:53,388
Nobody could move him.

81
00:03:53,487 --> 00:04:01,322
One evening, in the middle of sparring, my uncle stepped in and touched Kuribayashi's right side, no harder than tapping a melon.

82
00:04:01,421 --> 00:04:05,093
The big boy sat down on the mat with a strange look on his face.

83
00:04:05,193 --> 00:04:08,882
Uncle Mori turned to me and said, "Muscle is a coat, Reiko.

84
00:04:08,981 --> 00:04:10,983
Every coat has a gap under the arm.

85
00:04:11,084 --> 00:04:11,905
The lesson.

86
00:04:12,004 --> 00:04:14,256
You do not need to be stronger than his muscle.

87
00:04:14,355 --> 00:04:16,486
You only need to find the gap in his coat.

88
00:04:17,185 --> 00:04:19,048
But what if he is not standing still?

89
00:04:19,148 --> 00:04:20,807
What if he is running straight at you?

90
00:04:20,906 --> 00:04:24,062
Then there is a spot that lets his own speed do your work.

91
00:04:24,762 --> 00:04:25,697
Number two.

92
00:04:25,797 --> 00:04:27,074
The solar plexus.

93
00:04:27,173 --> 00:04:30,001
Find where your ribs meet in the middle of your chest.

94
00:04:30,100 --> 00:04:32,107
Now go about two fingers below it.

95
00:04:32,206 --> 00:04:34,346
Press there, and notice your breath catch.

96
00:04:34,446 --> 00:04:38,105
That soft spot is a bundle of nerves just under the surface.

97
00:04:38,204 --> 00:04:44,205
Have you ever been hit there, or fallen hard on your stomach, and for a few seconds you could not breathe at all?

98
00:04:44,305 --> 00:04:45,757
That is what he will feel.

99
00:04:46,456 --> 00:04:50,002
The wrong instinct when a big man charges is to back up.

100
00:04:50,101 --> 00:04:52,420
He is faster forward than you are backward.

101
00:04:52,519 --> 00:05:00,633
So instead, as he comes, bring your palm up into that spot, and hold your arm firm, like stopping a door that is swinging shut on you.

102
00:05:00,733 --> 00:05:02,063
Push slightly through him.

103
00:05:02,163 --> 00:05:03,759
You do not have to swing at all.

104
00:05:03,858 --> 00:05:07,208
His own weight and his own speed run straight into your hand.

105
00:05:07,307 --> 00:05:10,079
The one honest thing about this spot: it is small.

106
00:05:10,178 --> 00:05:12,567
An inch too high, and you hit breastbone.

107
00:05:12,666 --> 00:05:15,049
An inch to the side, and you hit ribs.

108
00:05:15,149 --> 00:05:16,885
Near the spot does very little.

109
00:05:16,985 --> 00:05:18,350
It has to be the spot.

110
00:05:19,050 --> 00:05:25,143
In my Saturday class, there is a woman named Bernice, seventy-four, who was a nurse for forty years.

111
00:05:25,242 --> 00:05:27,617
When I showed the class this spot, she laughed.

112
00:05:27,718 --> 00:05:29,507
"Reiko, I know that spot.

113
00:05:29,607 --> 00:05:32,730
In CPR, we teach people never to press there.

114
00:05:32,829 --> 00:05:35,105
Then she found it on herself in one try.

115
00:05:35,206 --> 00:05:37,173
Every other student took three or four.

116
00:05:37,273 --> 00:05:42,938
She looked at me and said, "So I've been carrying a weapon around for forty years, and nobody told me.

117
00:05:43,038 --> 00:05:43,859
The lesson.

118
00:05:43,959 --> 00:05:45,586
The target was always there.

119
00:05:45,685 --> 00:05:49,579
Knowing exactly where it is turns a small hand into a big answer.

120
00:05:50,278 --> 00:05:54,217
My men, when they rushed someone, counted on that person stepping back.

121
00:05:54,317 --> 00:05:59,349
A person who held their ground and put a hand out, they ran into it with all their own weight.

122
00:05:59,449 --> 00:06:01,021
Now, a question for you.

123
00:06:01,120 --> 00:06:04,014
If a big man is running at you, which would you choose?

124
00:06:04,113 --> 00:06:06,090
The liver, or the solar plexus?

125
00:06:06,189 --> 00:06:08,468
Write it in the comments, and tell me why.

126
00:06:08,567 --> 00:06:15,321
I will give you my answer in a minute, because the third spot, the one most people would never think of, may beat them both.

127
00:06:16,021 --> 00:06:16,858
Number one.

128
00:06:16,958 --> 00:06:17,716
The leg.

129
00:06:17,815 --> 00:06:19,581
Here is a secret about fights.

130
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:21,627
Almost every blow goes to the head.

131
00:06:21,726 --> 00:06:25,184
So his hands are up, and his eyes are up, watching your hands.

132
00:06:25,283 --> 00:06:27,092
Nobody is watching the legs.

133
00:06:27,192 --> 00:06:29,422
The wrong instinct comes from the movies.

134
00:06:29,521 --> 00:06:30,858
A high kick to the head.

135
00:06:30,958 --> 00:06:32,117
Please, do not.

136
00:06:32,218 --> 00:06:42,612
In real life, in slacks and shoes, with no warm-up, on concrete, at our age, the person who throws a movie kick is usually the person who ends up on the ground.

137
00:06:43,312 --> 00:06:44,424
So, you go low.

138
00:06:44,524 --> 00:06:46,461
Keep your foot no higher than a curb.

139
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:55,900
Swing your shin, or drive the bottom of your shoe into the outside of his thigh, halfway between his hip and his knee, like kicking a stuck cabinet door shut.

140
00:06:56,000 --> 00:07:00,293
Short, hard, and your foot is back on the ground before he knows what happened.

141
00:07:00,392 --> 00:07:02,008
You have felt this as a child.

142
00:07:02,108 --> 00:07:05,567
Somebody gave you a dead leg, and you could not run for a minute.

143
00:07:05,666 --> 00:07:06,826
That is the idea.

144
00:07:06,927 --> 00:07:09,081
A man with a dead leg cannot chase you.

145
00:07:09,180 --> 00:07:11,016
He cannot plant his feet to hit you.

146
00:07:11,117 --> 00:07:13,884
His balance goes, and his size goes with it.

147
00:07:13,983 --> 00:07:16,944
And you never stood on one leg for longer than a blink.

148
00:07:17,644 --> 00:07:20,547
I learned this one watching it happen to my own man.

149
00:07:20,646 --> 00:07:24,328
Shinsekai, Osaka, summer of 1981.

150
00:07:24,427 --> 00:07:29,637
One of our young men went to lean on an old fish seller, sixty-six, in white rubber boots.

151
00:07:29,737 --> 00:07:35,132
The young man was watching the old man's hands, because he thought the fish knife was the danger.

152
00:07:35,232 --> 00:07:37,261
The old man never touched the knife.

153
00:07:37,360 --> 00:07:42,052
He kicked my man once, low, in the side of the thigh, and went back to his fish.

154
00:07:42,151 --> 00:07:44,602
My man limped home and would not say why.

155
00:07:44,701 --> 00:07:46,479
We never went to that stall again.

156
00:07:46,579 --> 00:07:47,400
The lesson.

157
00:07:47,500 --> 00:07:49,424
The big man is watching your hands.

158
00:07:49,524 --> 00:07:50,640
Use your feet.

159
00:07:51,339 --> 00:07:55,015
Now, I promised you the one thing that tells you which spot to choose.

160
00:07:55,115 --> 00:07:56,189
It is his hands.

161
00:07:56,288 --> 00:07:58,456
My husband, Michio, taught me this.

162
00:07:58,555 --> 00:08:02,747
In my old life, we sometimes sat at dinners with very dangerous men.

163
00:08:02,846 --> 00:08:04,932
Michio never watched their faces.

164
00:08:05,031 --> 00:08:07,046
Afterward, he would tell me everything.

165
00:08:07,146 --> 00:08:08,885
"Reiko, faces lie.

166
00:08:08,985 --> 00:08:09,975
Hands don't.

167
00:08:10,076 --> 00:08:13,596
The man at the end of the table kept one hand under it all night.

168
00:08:13,696 --> 00:08:15,320
He was right, every time.

169
00:08:16,019 --> 00:08:17,468
So, watch his hands.

170
00:08:17,567 --> 00:08:21,561
If his hands are high, guarding his face, then his face is the wall.

171
00:08:21,661 --> 00:08:22,835
Do not hit the wall.

172
00:08:22,935 --> 00:08:27,251
Go to his body, his solar plexus and his liver, and go to his leg.

173
00:08:27,350 --> 00:08:30,088
If his hands drop low, his face is open.

174
00:08:30,187 --> 00:08:32,622
Then you may go high, but never the forehead.

175
00:08:32,721 --> 00:08:34,964
Go for the jaw, and never with a fist.

176
00:08:35,063 --> 00:08:40,473
Use the heel of your palm, fingers bent back, so the solid base of your hand does the work.

177
00:08:40,572 --> 00:08:41,745
It does not break.

178
00:08:41,846 --> 00:08:45,639
And if he is so close you cannot reach with your arm, use your elbow.

179
00:08:45,740 --> 00:08:46,827
Short and straight.

180
00:08:47,528 --> 00:08:48,976
Here is the scary truth.

181
00:08:49,076 --> 00:08:50,879
When it happens, you will not think.

182
00:08:50,980 --> 00:08:55,129
Your body does what it has already done a thousand times, and nothing else.

183
00:08:55,229 --> 00:09:04,493
Miyamoto Musashi, the greatest swordsman in Japanese history, wrote that a thousand days of training forge you, and ten thousand days polish you.

184
00:09:04,592 --> 00:09:06,565
You do not need ten thousand days.

185
00:09:06,664 --> 00:09:08,418
You need a few minutes every day.

186
00:09:09,118 --> 00:09:09,941
And the law.

187
00:09:10,041 --> 00:09:13,451
I am a black belt and a retired old crook, not your lawyer.

188
00:09:13,552 --> 00:09:15,514
Every state writes its own rules.

189
00:09:15,615 --> 00:09:19,831
You may defend yourself with force that fits the danger you are really in.

190
00:09:19,931 --> 00:09:23,147
The moment he stops, or turns, or runs, you stop.

191
00:09:23,246 --> 00:09:25,906
You do this to get free, never to get even.

192
00:09:26,005 --> 00:09:30,014
Then you get to people and light, and you call for help from somewhere safe.

193
00:09:30,115 --> 00:09:35,031
In my old life, the men who went to prison were not the ones who defended themselves.

194
00:09:35,130 --> 00:09:37,908
They were the ones who kept going after it was over.

195
00:09:38,009 --> 00:09:40,658
Remember that young man at Sannomiya Station.

196
00:09:41,359 --> 00:09:43,409
So here is the thing I promised.

197
00:09:43,509 --> 00:09:44,870
His hands decide.

198
00:09:44,970 --> 00:09:47,745
Hands high: solar plexus, liver, leg.

199
00:09:47,845 --> 00:09:50,614
Hands low: the heel of your palm to his jaw.

200
00:09:50,714 --> 00:09:52,205
Too close: your elbow.

201
00:09:52,304 --> 00:09:54,137
And never a bare fist to his head.

202
00:09:54,236 --> 00:09:55,724
My answer to the question?

203
00:09:55,823 --> 00:09:56,538
Neither.

204
00:09:56,639 --> 00:09:57,782
I choose the leg.

205
00:09:57,881 --> 00:09:59,459
It is the safest for you.

206
00:09:59,558 --> 00:10:01,516
It is the one he is not watching.

207
00:10:01,615 --> 00:10:03,576
And it works no matter how big he is.

208
00:10:04,277 --> 00:10:05,949
Here is your one thing this week.

209
00:10:06,048 --> 00:10:10,168
Fold a couch cushion and tape it to a doorframe at about stomach height.

210
00:10:10,269 --> 00:10:13,974
Every day, ten slow palm strikes into it, turning your hips.

211
00:10:14,073 --> 00:10:16,566
Then ten low kicks to the bottom of the frame.

212
00:10:16,666 --> 00:10:18,233
Foot no higher than a curb.

213
00:10:18,332 --> 00:10:19,558
Five minutes a day.

214
00:10:19,658 --> 00:10:22,864
Then tell me in the comments what changed after one week.

215
00:10:22,964 --> 00:10:27,060
And tell me, has anyone ever tried to push you around because they were bigger?

216
00:10:27,159 --> 00:10:28,452
How did you handle it?

217
00:10:28,552 --> 00:10:30,428
And what part of the country are you in?

218
00:10:30,528 --> 00:10:31,706
I read every one.

219
00:10:32,407 --> 00:10:37,028
If someone you love lives alone tonight, subscribe, and send them this video.

220
00:10:37,129 --> 00:10:39,865
I wish someone had shown Michio's mother these things.

221
00:10:39,965 --> 00:10:48,527
The video on your screen now is the one about beating a bigger man, and what a seventy-one-year-old noodle cook did to my biggest enforcer.

222
00:10:48,626 --> 00:10:50,000
Watch that one next.

223
00:10:50,100 --> 00:10:51,091
Lock your door.

224
00:10:51,192 --> 00:10:52,076
Live long.

225
00:10:52,177 --> 00:10:53,552
I will see you next time.
